   $q$Which detail does the narrator share about the hummingbird's private thinking?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She asked the heron how he could stand there doing nothing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-dialogue-with-thought"},{"text":"She had visited fifty flowers since the sun came up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-dialogue-with-thought"},{"text":"She drooped onto a reed beside the heron in the afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-action-with-thought"},{"text":"She was sure that being fast was the only way to get things done.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She was sure that being fast was the only way to get things done.$q$, $q$The narrator tells us "She was sure that being fast was the only way," which is a belief she never says out loud. Her question to the heron is spoken dialogue, not a private thought.$q$, 'draft', '60431ae8-50d8-5029-856d-eb8f1056461c')
